pe":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n- I have tested it on Windows 10, not sure about other OS\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9579) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the Minimal reproduction project, there are two confirmation dialogs, one is a child of the other, and a button that pops the child dialog. The child dialog has an additional `Always on Top` flag enabled. Also, The property `display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows = false` for this project\n\nNow whenever, I open (and then close) the sub window, all later attempts at confirming (or cancelling) the parent window makes it unresponsive.\n\nNote: I don't think it's relevant but the error that appears in debugger in video is:\n```\nE 0:00:05:092   window_set_transient: Windows with the 'on top' can't become transient.\n  <C++ Error>   Condition \"wd_window.always_on_top\" is true.\n  <C++ Source>  platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp:2207 @ window_set_transient()\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/484503de-84d5-4e3d-8608-a0aeb3c7d485\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Run the MRP\n- Click \"Open FileDialog\" button (the button text is irrelevant). A child dialog will pop up.\n- Close the child dialog.\n- Try to close the parent dialog. The app will become unresponsive\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[new-game-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26155923/new-game-project.zip)","closed_by":{"log